        "original_id": "1643c0b9-ca34-55da-82a6-979ce04832d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Antonio Machado, Miriam Toews, Carlos Falcó\n- Places: Palacio de las Dueñas, Steinbach, Manitoba\n- Works: Irma Voth, A Complicated Kindness, All My Puny Sorrows\n- Concepts: Generation of '98\n\nFacts:\n- Antonio Machado was born on 26 July 1875 and died on 22 February 1939.\n- Antonio Machado was a Spanish poet and a leading figure of the Generation of '98 literary movement.\n- Antonio Machado was born at the Palacio de las Dueñas.\n- Carlos Falcó, Marqués de Griñón and Marqués de Castelmoncayo, was also born at the Palacio de las Dueñas.\n- Miriam Toews was born in 1964 in Steinbach, Manitoba, and she is a Canadian writer.\n- Miriam Toews is best known for the novels A Complicated Kindness and All My Puny Sorrows.\n- Irma Voth is the fifth novel by Canadian author Miriam Toews.",
